    <description>DWDECI-40/92. Quick-Action-launched screen flow for logging a Business Incident (RecordAlert) against the current record (Business Account, Scholar Person Account, or Course Offering Participant). Category is a plain picklist of the 3 real category names, not a live lookup - RecordAlertCategory.SobjectType is excluded from the ObjectPermissions restricted picklist, so no non-Admin profile can ever browse/select it directly via a native lookup. The actual real RecordAlertCategory record is resolved and the RecordAlert is created by the RecordAlert_Autolaunched_Commit_Business_Incident subflow, which runs in system context to bypass that restriction. What defaults to the logging user ($User.Id), since WhatId is a required field with no defined business meaning in this design and must differ from Parent.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>RecordAlert - Screen Flow - Log Business Incident {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
